<a href="http://gangrey.com/1116">
<h2 class="design">Making It Up?</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">B.S. dept.</h4>

<p>

This time it's allegations against Scott Thomas Beauchamp in the New Republic.<br />
<br />
<a href="http://www.foxnews.com/story/0,2933,292367,00.html">The Weekly Standard</a> <i>has learned from a military source close to the investigation that Pvt. Scott Thomas Beauchamp -- author of the much-disputed "Shock Troops" article in the New Republic's July 23 issue as well as two previous "Baghdad Diarist" columns -- signed a sworn statement admitting that all three articles he published in the New Republic were exaggerations and falsehoods -- fabrications containing only "a smidgen of truth," in the words of our source.</i><br />
<br />
The <a href="http://www.tnr.com/">New Republic</a>, <a href="httphttp://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_Glass">um</a>, <a href="http://www.tnr.com/blog/the_plank?pid=132739">is standing by Beauchamp.</a><br />
<br />
Lest we forget, tell the truth.
